  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.04877v1</id>
    <title>Frequency of a Digit in the Representation of a Number and the Asymptotic Mean Value of the Digits</title>
    <updated>2026-03-05T07:07:01Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.04877v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.04877v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We study the relationship between the frequency of a ternary digit in a number and the asymptotic mean value of the digits. The conditions for the existence of the asymptotic mean of digits in a ternary number are established. We indicate an infinite everywhere dense set of numbers without frequency of digits but with the asymptotic mean of the digits.</summary>
    <category term="math.NT" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="math.FA" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
